atrix contains three zeros, more than any other row. So using a Laplace expansion along the $4$th row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 11 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 6 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{41}+(-2)\\cdot {C}_{42}+0\\cdot {C}_{43}+0\\cdot {C}_{44} \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-1)^{4+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 8\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-69952/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a88f6712-2115-55ce-abe4-b3c27e2e105f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-69952"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-77800/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "3c1595ed-d8f5-552e-8664-20f16fd916f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77800/selection/e0e0a3ac4fe95f021c8f8aece7092270d36ad30c356733db1e628dc4f0b1d434" :answer/id #uuid "36d3a662-6530-5790-a658-73b6b5bea937" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77800/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer/id #uuid "a430bcc2-9907-54ec-8a56-cc5eeed5f638" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77800/selection/f4f7e304b38327904d9fdebbac3479cccadb547b1c29d7b8e5938e7012f9d65b" :answer/id #uuid "05559a09-9dd8-5cb5-ad32-0e96d722521f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77800/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer/id #uuid "f52a1fb8-5907-5281-9da6-7cdfbd4271cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77800/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9ce55b07-8fc2-5678-b9fa-9bc66f752c9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-77800/selection/f4f7e304b38327904d9fdebbac3479cccadb547b1c29d7b8e5938e7012f9d65b" :answer-field/choices ["q-77800/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" "q-77800/selection/e0e0a3ac4fe95f021c8f8aece7092270d36ad30c356733db1e628dc4f0b1d434" "q-77800/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" "q-77800/selection/f4f7e304b38327904d9fdebbac3479cccadb547b1c29d7b8e5938e7012f9d65b" "q-77800/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-77800" :question/id #uuid "bc2737ad-9661-5058-a34f-99a5440f4b8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-77800" :question/problem "Compute the following determinant using a cofactor expansion along the $2$nd row:\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}|.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using cofactor expansion along the $2$nd row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{21}+0\\cdot {C}_{22}+0\\cdot {C}_{23}+3\\cdot {C}_{24} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{2+4}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $1$st row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{11}+(-1)\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{1+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-7-0 \\\\  & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}|=3(-7)=-21.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-77800/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1637e23-6566-5e45-af4c-b27333f882d1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-77800"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-77802/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer/id #uuid "65e1c48a-a17c-503f-9bcb-2f4956fc6ac5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77802/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "979174bf-18d7-5b7a-ab0f-c6e68bc4a137" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77802/selection/4644593a6ae896793c595e8a37cd468ba91be6a8038e715c4c88cddad1968793" :answer/id #uuid "b67dfd61-89c0-54f9-977c-2c60f5dd11bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77802/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "753f6780-0984-554b-9b23-69e36a0c9027" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77802/selection/f4f7e304b38327904d9fdebbac3479cccadb547b1c29d7b8e5938e7012f9d65b" :answer/id #uuid "9478810b-076e-5574-b2b8-e913ee91e5aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77802/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1f6ccf54-98d1-58f4-b577-8321d09bf3d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-77802/selection/f4f7e304b38327904d9fdebbac3479cccadb547b1c29d7b8e5938e7012f9d65b" :answer-field/choices ["q-77802/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" "q-77802/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" "q-77802/selection/4644593a6ae896793c595e8a37cd468ba91be6a8038e715c4c88cddad1968793" "q-77802/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" "q-77802/selection/f4f7e304b38327904d9fdebbac3479cccadb547b1c29d7b8e5938e7012f9d65b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-77802" :question/id #uuid "f62396c6-1691-5457-8833-10a94ba78d86" :question/math-academy-id "q-77802" :question/problem "Compute the following determinant using a cofactor expansion along the $4$th row:\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using cofactor expansion along the $4$th row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =-2\\cdot {C}_{41}+5\\cdot {C}_{42}+0\\cdot {C}_{43}+0\\cdot {C}_{44} \\\\  & =-2\\cdot (-1)^{4+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}|+5\\cdot (-1)^{4+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}|+5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the first $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $1$st row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}| & =(-1)\\cdot {C}_{11}+1\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -7 & 4\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot (-1)^{1+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -7 & 4\\end{aligned}|-|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(-4-7)-(-8+2) \\\\  & =11+6 \\\\  & =17\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the second  $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $1$st row, we obtain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 4\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot {C}_{11}+1\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -7 & 4\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot (-1)^{1+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -7 & 4\\end{aligned}|-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-4-7)-(0+0) \\\\  & =-11-0 \\\\  & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|=2(17)+5(-11)=-21.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-77802/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d1637e23-6566-5e45-af4c-b27333f882d1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-77802"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-42104/selection/5a1d390dd885ba58c71510dd810aa79a0ad3f39d34596e86904c0b57c6d82b8f" :answer/id #uuid "273adc09-026f-5fa2-a648-7061fc911458" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42104/selection/ef64417d1a2cdf52c790fa828d4b81830db83d8e558bc3c0b58bd178ddccf04f" :answer/id #uuid "ee0495ae-d5ad-5532-a427-999f8a2bd406" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42104/selection/5811619417b7df81d29ce639151dfa2793857d57c1dd8fccc8c6ee0107818b79" :answer/id #uuid "f2c054c6-5ccd-5f9b-8e6e-e217fd3c728e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42104/selection/46322932ccd2d84da6fc7c8a315772e85246c45a300d19f40a23a9c29cd34826" :answer/id #uuid "bf83fa31-0c02-5802-a33e-fc1154d974b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42104/selection/3cb26798e39a4b8581e45834dc01f210df3331b6fdf3f51b6e7d5285bcfe2827" :answer/id #uuid "b8826dd7-3f60-515a-b512-54910c3c5260" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42104/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3415debb-5d3e-5508-8ea1-fa07f59cfc4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-42104/selection/5811619417b7df81d29ce639151dfa2793857d57c1dd8fccc8c6ee0107818b79" :answer-field/choices ["q-42104/selection/5a1d390dd885ba58c71510dd810aa79a0ad3f39d34596e86904c0b57c6d82b8f" "q-42104/selection/ef64417d1a2cdf52c790fa828d4b81830db83d8e558bc3c0b58bd178ddccf04f" "q-42104/selection/5811619417b7df81d29ce639151dfa2793857d57c1dd8fccc8c6ee0107818b79" "q-42104/selection/46322932ccd2d84da6fc7c8a315772e85246c45a300d19f40a23a9c29cd34826" "q-42104/selection/3cb26798e39a4b8581e45834dc01f210df3331b6fdf3f51b6e7d5285bcfe2827"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-42104" :question/id #uuid "9e1a0ecf-c99d-5b41-851f-c3bc683d9006" :question/math-academy-id "q-42104" :question/problem "$|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5 & -1\\end{aligned}|=$" :question/worked-solution "Using a cofactor expansion along the $4$th column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{14}+2\\cdot {C}_{24}+0\\cdot {C}_{34}+(-1)\\cdot {C}_{44} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{2+4}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{4+4}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-42104/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db6f57f3-d9f0-5ea7-a557-e729a8c0777f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-42104"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-42103/selection/0fbd722a430fb27be2142edd2608e0fcea446f6dcf6528dcc65d1523b1e4a8b7" :answer/id #uuid "02cf0eb7-d6e9-50f1-93a0-a79d424730f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42103/selection/4cb156920b3a2ef721f751b1e662786ed9553c3a259b52bad0634c38085b7d86" :answer/id #uuid "dae30ebb-0d51-58bf-977d-a7cb2ef3e838" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42103/selection/38e8eb4b361bb0aabc82907b766c3ae0d17cb3de9534e826d48aa211eaeffafc" :answer/id #uuid "f12cbe05-fd9d-5e6b-b4ae-0ec3666a80e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42103/selection/81f1e4405a455414858d968e8152cbe51fc200694d8eea5615b4c52e679b7c3a" :answer/id #uuid "17ab7d32-d287-5c28-8efd-8ca4c083ade0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42103/selection/974c63a60bfb272ffcd3046b3d8cdb0d2e1cc451fd339522d2a9c0309c90d350" :answer/id #uuid "640dfa86-aa74-585f-8886-e7661a11d179" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42103/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "54c02883-f45d-5a77-a4cd-81426c52e0fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-42103/selection/0fbd722a430fb27be2142edd2608e0fcea446f6dcf6528dcc65d1523b1e4a8b7" :answer-field/choices ["q-42103/selection/0fbd722a430fb27be2142edd2608e0fcea446f6dcf6528dcc65d1523b1e4a8b7" "q-42103/selection/4cb156920b3a2ef721f751b1e662786ed9553c3a259b52bad0634c38085b7d86" "q-42103/selection/38e8eb4b361bb0aabc82907b766c3ae0d17cb3de9534e826d48aa211eaeffafc" "q-42103/selection/81f1e4405a455414858d968e8152cbe51fc200694d8eea5615b4c52e679b7c3a" "q-42103/selection/974c63a60bfb272ffcd3046b3d8cdb0d2e1cc451fd339522d2a9c0309c90d350"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-42103" :question/id #uuid "73e3a5dc-c1a1-5e2b-83f6-824330db6d36" :question/math-academy-id "q-42103" :question/problem "$|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|=$" :question/worked-solution "Using a cofactor expansion along the $3$rd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{13}+1\\cdot {C}_{23}+0\\cdot {C}_{33}+0\\cdot {C}_{43} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+3}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-42103/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db6f57f3-d9f0-5ea7-a557-e729a8c0777f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-42103"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-77806/selection/f87b94d4559399370d59a91ed2afa8bd0a9042f8b3b85e02a2ef62b03399067b" :answer/id #uuid "444fb401-6c4a-5bd5-9a1e-9dc8ed56148d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & -7 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77806/selection/f6faec3613cf09a63dbe40dcd02f8764d03f9b55d7da897f641f741fb5764615" :answer/id #uuid "00762f5b-51e4-5c77-bc6e-20f41210a969" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & -7 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77806/selection/18190bf2f085b2d082cdb8533c8019222113ef44dc39839f348a369a09107280" :answer/id #uuid "61db11bd-cec7-5d6c-bdd7-b55c51e8faba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}5 & -7 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77806/selection/0c7b67e39e063832872f8f5ca3cef2f5719ca6dda777b20aadb01c3cbc383b05" :answer/id #uuid "33202255-27b3-5a92-974f-4189a012fcd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}5 & -7 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77806/selection/029aa0fdcc28abb73d5599f2ec64d78b70866ab9c07118f98f89896b6650d0fd" :answer/id #uuid "50b9fcb0-8034-52ce-9cda-328a7d3c908d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & -7 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-77806/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "412e1a77-a5b5-5650-884b-ab1e9fd97910" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-77806/selection/029aa0fdcc28abb73d5599f2ec64d78b70866ab9c07118f98f89896b6650d0fd" :answer-field/choices ["q-77806/selection/f87b94d4559399370d59a91ed2afa8bd0a9042f8b3b85e02a2ef62b03399067b" "q-77806/selection/f6faec3613cf09a63dbe40dcd02f8764d03f9b55d7da897f641f741fb5764615" "q-77806/selection/18190bf2f085b2d082cdb8533c8019222113ef44dc39839f348a369a09107280" "q-77806/selection/0c7b67e39e063832872f8f5ca3cef2f5719ca6dda777b20aadb01c3cbc383b05" "q-77806/selection/029aa0fdcc28abb73d5599f2ec64d78b70866ab9c07118f98f89896b6650d0fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-77806" :question/id #uuid "01d90be8-dd13-5769-8e95-4a16276c217c" :question/math-academy-id "q-77806" :question/problem "$|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|=$" :question/worked-solution "Using a cofactor expansion along the $1$st column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =-2\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{21}+0\\cdot {C}_{31}+0\\cdot {C}_{41} \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & -7 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & -7 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 8 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-77806/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db6f57f3-d9f0-5ea7-a557-e729a8c0777f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-77806"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5182"] :question/problem "Using a cofactor expansion along the $4$th row, write the following determinant as a combination of $3 \\times 3$ determinants:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/assets/502b9464378fb5030a72918f45938184f120773e4639f3f50f071ca82fc307ce.png)" :question/worked-solution "Using a Laplace expansion along the $4$th row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 7 & 9 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -6 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =(-6)\\cdot {C}_{41}+0\\cdot {C}_{42}+0\\cdot {C}_{43}+1\\cdot {C}_{44} \\\\  & =(-6)\\cdot (-1)^{4+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 9 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot (-1)^{4+4}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =6\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 7 & 9 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/assets/a1c11cfd7d1cacae0881118776eb6b38dea7b92c4f542e8158e31bbfa59274ec.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4418"] :question/problem "Calculate\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/assets/15738eec7022be44c90577b931f2e8aa8446a8fc3f911260fcf468ae6ddd2d57.png)" :question/worked-solution "The $4$th row of the matrix contains three zeros, more than any other row. So using a Laplace expansion along the $4$th row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{41}+0\\cdot {C}_{42}+0\\cdot {C}_{43}+(-1)\\cdot {C}_{44} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{4+4}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the $3 \\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $1$st row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|+|\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3-8)+(0-0) \\\\  & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/assets/ce96c053abb756977f717e7130257af39307e5f663596042ddcb5b14b0153cb8.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4419"] :question/problem "Using a cofactor expansion along the $2$nd column, write the following determinant as a combination of $3 \\times 3$ determinants:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/assets/82b151cbc7d19f4afa375763d0ca8eb281d76e11f2d775c068e97dbf3d40cae4.png)" :question/worked-solution "Using a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd column, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{12}+3\\cdot {C}_{22}+0\\cdot {C}_{32}+0\\cdot {C}_{42} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14081343/assets/efb849ac6e240be4d0a6aac3e7f9405158b8b1bb996956b7346c02b5bee751b1.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
